  "leProgram": "% Logical English reading of \"Software Licence (sample)\", revision 1, generated by the word authoring POC.\n% Profile wap-le-forms 0.1.0. Not checked by an LE parser.\n\nthe templates are:\n    *a party* shall *an activity* within *a period*.\n    *a party* shall not *an activity*.\n    *a party* shall *an activity*.\n    *a party* may terminate *an activity*.\n    *a party* may *an activity*.\n    *a party* is not liable for *a matter*.\n    *a term* means *a description*.\n\nthe knowledge base software_licence includes:\n\n% 1.1 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cLicensor\u201d means the party granting rights under this Agreement.\n\n% 1.2 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cLicensee\u201d means the party receiving rights under this Agreement.\n\n% 1.3 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cSoftware\u201d means the computer program licensed under this Agreement.\n\n% 1.4 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cDocumentation\u201d means the user manuals supplied with the Software.\n\n% 2.1 Permission (form permission)\nLicensee may use the Software for its internal business purposes.\n\n% 2.2 Permission (form permission)\nLicensee may permit up to 10 users to access the Software.\n\n% 2.3 Prohibition (form prohibition)\nLicensee shall not sublicense the Software.\n\n% 3.1 Prohibition (form prohibition)\nLicensee shall not reverse engineer the Software.\n\n% 4.1 Obligation (form obligation)\nLicensee shall pay the GBP 5,000 annually in advance.\n\n% 4.2 Obligation (form obligation-within)\nLicensee shall pay each invoice within 30 days.\n\n% 5.1 Exclusion (form exclusion-not-liable)\nLicensor is not liable for any loss of profits.\n\n% 6.1 Power (form power-terminate)\nLicensor may terminate this Agreement if Licensee fails to pay any fee.\n",
